# Code style

- Use **full, clear names** for variables, methods, classes, and files (`incomingFreightPoints`, `originTownRecord`, `freightTransporterIdentifiers`). Avoid cryptic abbreviations (`p`, `d`, `a`, `b`, `tmp`) except very local loop indexes where context is obvious.
- **Comments**: do not saturate the code with inline comments. Document only what is **non-obvious** or **complex** (business rules, tradeoffs, external API limits). Do not comment every basic function.
- All source code (identifiers, comments, file names, packages) must be in **English**. No Spanish or Spanglish in code. User-visible UI copy stays in Spanish, sentence case.
